# =============================================================================
# oc-swap — the SWAP/install leg of the four-way oc-deploy split.
#
# Owns the `swap-execute` verb: the Phase B body that downloads the artifact the
# carrier run built, verifies it, backs up + installs the binary, bounces the
# daemon, publishes the fork release, stamps the ledger, notifies, and writes
# the receipt — under a host-wide flock, and re-exec'd out of the unit cgroup so
# the bounce cannot SIGKILL steps 9-12 (the v0.4.153 silent-ledger defect).
#
# WHAT MOVED HERE, VERBATIM (byte-slices of oc-deploy@5f81c599):
#   swap_in_bounce_cgroup, swap_ensure_detached   (source 269-311)
#   the swap-execute banner comment               (source 1362-1365)
#   swap_execute (+ the hoisted sidecar_sync and
#    post_verify)                                 (source 1498-1886)
#   the `swap-execute)` dispatch arm              (source 2732-2752)
# Nothing was rewritten and no rc was re-mapped. Config, journal, ledger stamp,
# receipts, backup pruning, the fork-release identity and the argv loop are
# SHARED and live in tools/lib/oc-deploy-lib.sh.
#
# RETRACTED (corrected 2026-11-22, factory#142). This header used to carry a
# "KNOWN LATENT DEFECT" claiming post_verify() calls `$PV_MAT` where the variable
# is `PV_MATCH`. Every part of that was false, and the note was itself the ONLY
